   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend chapter 670 of the laws of 2024 relating to authorizing the\nlease of certain lands for the Albany NanoTech Complex, in relation to\nprohibiting the state university of New York from contracting out certain\nservices",
    "basePrintNo": "S7409",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S7409-2025",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Add §5-a, Chap 670 of 2024",
    "lawSection": "Conveyance of State Land",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S7409\n\nSPONSOR: FAHY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend chapter 670 of the laws of 2024 relating to authorizing\nthe lease of certain lands for the Albany NanoTech Complex, in relation\nto prohibiting the state university of New York from contracting out\ncertain services\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nTo ensure that the lease of certain lands at SUNY Albany does not\ndisplace any state employees or waive or impair any state employee\nrights or benefits.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection one would provide that neither SUNY nor an entity affiliated or\nassociated with SUNY shall contract out to the Fuller Road Management\nCorporation, subsidiary of such corporation, or the SUNY Research Foun-\ndation for services or privatize any services currently performed by\nunclassified SONY Albany employees working at the Albany NanoTech\nComplex. This section would also provide that nothing within Chapter 670\nof the Laws of 2024 related to the lease of SONY Albany property to a\nprivate entity for the development, construction, or operation or facil-\nities shall waive or impair any rights or benefits of SONY employees.\n\nSection two would provide the effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nThis bill would provide necessary clarification of Chapter 670 of the\nLaws of 2024 to ensure its effective implementation.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS FOR STATE AND LOCAL GOVERNMENTS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act would take effect immediately.\n",
